    "summary": "(Register 1964)\r\nComposite stringed instrument; half a calabash covered with skin forms the resonator, its circular opening is covered with snake or lizard skin, with a hole at one side. The strings consist of a bunch of horse hair secured at the top of the neck by a leather thong; the end of the thong hangs down and has a cowrie shell threaded on the end; to be played as a fiddle with a bow.",
